{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Online Dating"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Sweet Conversation"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way.  <br/><br/> You use Present Perfect Continuous tense to describe:  <ul><li>a single activity that lasts a long time, and</li><li>  an action that is repeated over a long period of time.</li></ul> These continue up to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I have learned English </span>= I learned English in the past and now I can speak English. <br/><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect Continuous tense when a long activity has just stopped."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the action, use the continuous form.<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul> <li>I've been coming here every week since I started my new job. </li> <li> Have you been dating a lot since you joined Tender?</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the result of the action, use the simple form.<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> I've always felt at home here. </li><li> I've been on a few dates.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Has/Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb+ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  coming here every week <span class=\\\"strong\\\">since</span> I started my new job.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, six years etc.)</li><li> You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Monday, she was a child)</li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bookmark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to save information online for later use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you like a profile, you can also bookmark it in your list of favorites."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compatible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "capable of existing together in harmony or in peace"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm not compatible with most of the guys who like me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "daunting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "difficult to deal with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Speed dating can be a daunting experience at first."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to have good chemistry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to share many things in common with someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you have good chemistry with someone, you'll know straight away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comfort zone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a situation in which you feel the most at ease"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You shouldn't get out of your comfort zone on the first date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "captivated "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "showing great attraction to something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to feel captivated by a conversation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in common"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " sharing many interests"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have been talking to this girl, and we have so many things in common! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob11aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use <span class=\"italic\">I wish ... \u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense. <br/><br/> I wish I knew ... <br/> I wish I had ... <br/> I wish you were ... <br/><br/>Structure: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I wish I knew more people like me.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to know more people like me but I don't know them.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I wish I could find someone who has good chemistry with me.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to know someone who has good chemistry with me but I don't anyone like that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  I wish I could keep my dates captivated for more than one evening! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to keep my dates captivated but that's not the case.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (12-14 lines) with a partner about a first date."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of 3 or 4 questions that you would ask your date in order to get to know them better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of 3 or 4 things that describe you. Try to think about things that make you unique  or original."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the things you have in common, and share your opinions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your dialogue aloud to another group."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I have done and what I have been doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "